hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1327","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Mu’alla bin Asad told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Al-Aflat bin Khalifa told us, Jasra bint told me A chicken, she said: I heard Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came with the faces of his companions’ homes facing the mosque. He said: “Face these houses away from the mosque.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered, but the people did not do anything. He hoped that it would come down to them in That was a concession, so he came out to them after that and said: “Face these houses away from the mosque, for I do not make the mosque lawful for a menstruating woman or a woman in a state of sexual impurity.”"
